      "scene_type": "gs_numbers",
      "spoken": "The Grossglockner High Alpine Road in Austria crosses the Hohe Tauern range. Its highest point, at the Hochtor, sits at 2,504 metres. On average, there is a hairpin every 1.3 kilometres. The highest point you can drive to is the Edelweissspitze at 2,571 metres.",
